From 48b9400989adaf91613c6a82dde1956815c9f597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 22:03:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0107 -- SB 8-bit DMA path -> MONO output + ring
 silence-prime

The SDL/0106 graceful 8-bit-DMA fall-back unblocked audio on a PicoGUS in
SB mode (g2k iter wpgsb1: IRQ-5 fires, the 8-bit low-DMA D-channel path is
selected), but the 8-bit path itself opened the device SB-Pro STEREO: for a
DSP >= 3 card it set channels=2, doubled the time-constant byte rate via the
0x40 time constant, and wrote the SB-Pro 0x0E stereo mixer bit. A PicoGUS in
SB mode and a real SB 2.0 report DSP 3.x/4.x but do NOT implement SB-Pro
alternate-byte stereo demux, so that program plays at the wrong effective
rate -- music came out ~an octave too high ("chipmunk") with distortion.
Separately the software ring buffer is SDL_calloc-zeroed to 0x00, which is
correct silence for S16 (16-bit) but is full-negative DC for U8 (8-bit), so
on the 8-bit path the ring played a loud pop/"static-burst" before the
loading screen until the first real fill landed.

Why DOS needs this: the pre-SB16 8-bit path must not assume SB-Pro stereo.
Two fixes, both scoped strictly to the 8-bit branch:

  1. MONO by default. The 8-bit format/channel select now opens channels=1
     (U8 mono). The shared effective_rate = channels*freq time-constant
     formula then yields tc = 256 - 1000000/freq (no channel doubling;
     11025 -> tc=166, effective=11025), and the 0x0E stereo mixer bit is
     gated on the actual channels==2 so MONO leaves it unwritten. SDL's
     logical->physical audiostream downmixes the engine's (mono-content)
     app stream to the mono device losslessly.
  2. Ring silence-prime. At OpenDevice, after the ring is allocated and
     before the 0xD1 speaker-on + 0x1C auto-init DMA start, the software
     ring is memset to soundblaster_silence_value (0x80 on this path).
     Gated on !is_sb16.

Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_8BIT_STEREO=1 (strict-"1", default 0)
restores the prior SB-Pro 8-bit STEREO program (channels=2 + 0x0E bit) for a
genuine SB Pro (DSP 3.x) that supports it; a DSP < 3 card has no SB-Pro
stereo so the flag cannot force it there.

BYTE-IDENTICAL for the 16-bit SB16 path (is_sb16==true, Vibra16): all SDL/0107
code lives inside the `else` (8-bit) branch of the format/channel select and
under `if (!is_sb16)` for the ring prime; the is_sb16 branch sets S16LE/ch=2
exactly as before, no SDL_GetHint runs on that path, and no ring memset is
added (its silence value is 0x00, already produced by the calloc). DOSBox-X
emulates an SB16 so it stays on the 16-bit path and is unaffected.

Diagnostics: a new always-on (8-bit-branch) banner
  audio: SDL/0107 8-bit channel mode: ch=N (MONO|STEREO) tc=T effective=E Hz
  stereo_bit=(yes|no) ring_silence_primed=yes ...
lets build-qa/g2k witness ch=1 / MONO / no-stereo-bit / silence-primed. The
existing SDL/0106 8-bit DSP-start-seq banner's stereo-bit suffix now keys on
channels==2 (not DSP>=3) so it stays accurate. The new banner is an OPTIONAL
smoke entry (8-bit-only; DOSBox-X SB16 never runs the branch).

Workspace-local patch; not upstreamed (sdl_ai_policy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 96 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 80 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 842d14040..c72d4cf1a 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -2351,15 +2351,42 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         // SB16 (DSP >= 4): 16-bit stereo signed
         device->spec.format = SDL_AUDIO_S16LE;
         device->spec.channels = 2;
-    } else if (soundblaster_version >= 3) {
-        // SB Pro (DSP 3.x): 8-bit stereo unsigned.
-        // Max 22050 Hz in stereo (hardware interleaves L/R at double the rate).
-        device->spec.format = SDL_AUDIO_U8;
-        device->spec.channels = 2;
     } else {
-        // SB 2.0 (DSP 2.x) and SB 1.x: 8-bit mono unsigned.
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0107): 8-bit (pre-SB16) channel mode. DEFAULT =
+           MONO. The pre-patch code opened SB-Pro alternate-byte STEREO whenever
+           the DSP reported >= 3 (channels=2 + the 2x-byte-rate time constant +
+           the 0x0E stereo mixer bit). A PicoGUS-in-SB-mode card and a real SB
+           2.0 report DSP 3.x/4.x but do NOT implement SB-Pro alternate-byte
+           stereo demux, so that stereo program plays at the wrong effective
+           rate (chipmunk pitch) + distortion on g2k. Open MONO instead: the
+           time constant becomes 256 - 1000000/freq (no channel doubling; the
+           shared effective_rate = channels*freq formula yields freq for ch=1),
+           the 0x0E stereo bit is left unwritten (below), and SDL's logical->
+           physical audiostream downmixes the (already mono-content) app stream
+           to the mono device losslessly.
+
+           Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_8BIT_STEREO=1 (strict-"1",
+           default 0) restores the prior SB-Pro 8-bit STEREO program for a
+           genuine SB Pro (DSP >= 3) that DOES support it. A DSP < 3 card has no
+           SB-Pro stereo at all, so the killswitch cannot force stereo there
+           (matches the pre-patch SB 2.0 / 1.x mono behavior). All SDL/0107 new
+           code lives inside this else (8-bit) branch -- the is_sb16 (16-bit)
+           path above is byte-identical to pre-0107. */
+        const char *sb8_stereo_hint =
+            SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_8BIT_STEREO");
+        const bool sb_8bit_stereo =
+            (sb8_stereo_hint && sb8_stereo_hint[0] == '1' && sb8_stereo_hint[1] == '\0');
+
         device->spec.format = SDL_AUDIO_U8;
-        device->spec.channels = 1;
+        if (sb_8bit_stereo && soundblaster_version >= 3) {
+            // Killswitch ON: prior SB Pro (DSP 3.x) 8-bit STEREO (L/R interleaved
+            // at 2x the per-channel byte rate; the 0x0E stereo bit is set below).
+            device->spec.channels = 2;
+        } else {
+            // Default: 8-bit MONO -- correct effective rate on PicoGUS-SB /
+            // real SB 2.0 (no SB-Pro stereo demux); also the DSP < 3 mono path.
+            device->spec.channels = 1;
+        }
     }
 
     // Accept whatever frequency SDL3's audio layer passes in. For SB16 (DSP >= 4)
@@ -2698,6 +2725,22 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     isr_is_16bit = is_sb16;
     isr_silence_value = soundblaster_silence_value;
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0107): silence-prime the software ring buffer on the
+       8-bit (U8) path BEFORE the speaker turns on (0xD1) and the auto-init DMA
+       starts (0x1C). SDL_calloc above zero-fills the ring to 0x00, which is the
+       correct silence value for S16LE (16-bit) but is FULL-NEGATIVE DC for U8
+       -- so on the 8-bit path any ring bytes consumed before the SDL audio
+       thread first fills real audio play as a loud pop/static burst (heard on
+       g2k before the loading screen). Re-prime to the U8 silence value (0x80,
+       == soundblaster_silence_value on this path). Gated on !is_sb16 so the
+       16-bit path is byte-identical to pre-0107 (its silence value is 0x00,
+       already produced by the calloc; no memset is added on that path). The
+       DMA double-buffer is separately primed to soundblaster_silence_value at
+       allocation above; this covers the ring that feeds it. */
+    if (!is_sb16) {
+        SDL_memset(hidden->ring_buffer, soundblaster_silence_value, hidden->ring_size);
+    }
+
     // Lock all ISR code and data to prevent page faults during interrupts.
     DOS_LockCode(SoundBlasterIRQHandler, SoundBlasterIRQHandler_End);
     DOS_LockCode(RingCopyOut, RingCopyOut_End);
@@ -2918,16 +2961,19 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         WriteSoundBlasterDSP(0x40); // set time constant
         WriteSoundBlasterDSP(time_constant);
 
-        // SB Pro (DSP 3.x): enable or disable stereo via mixer register 0x0E
-        if (soundblaster_version >= 3) {
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0107): program the SB-Pro stereo mixer bit (0x0E)
+           ONLY when actually opening 8-bit STEREO (the SB_8BIT_STEREO killswitch
+           path on a genuine DSP >= 3 SB Pro -> channels == 2). The default MONO
+           path leaves 0x0E untouched: PicoGUS-in-SB-mode / real SB 2.0 do not
+           implement SB-Pro stereo and the register is meaningless to them.
+           For every pre-0107 code path channels == 2 iff the old `version >= 3`
+           gate selected stereo, so the genuine-SB-Pro stereo program is
+           byte-identical (select 0x0E, set bit 1). */
+        if (device->spec.channels == 2) {
             const int mixer_addr = soundblaster_base_port + 0x04;
             const int mixer_data = soundblaster_base_port + 0x05;
             outportb(mixer_addr, 0x0E); // select output/stereo register
-            if (device->spec.channels == 2) {
-                outportb(mixer_data, inportb(mixer_data) | 0x02); // set bit 1 = stereo
-            } else {
-                outportb(mixer_data, inportb(mixer_data) & ~0x02); // clear bit 1 = mono
-            }
+            outportb(mixer_data, inportb(mixer_data) | 0x02); // set bit 1 = stereo
         }
 
         // start 8-bit auto-initialize DMA mode
@@ -2945,13 +2991,31 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
            the 8-bit (pre-SB16 / PicoGUS-SB / SB2.0-class) path. This is the
            sequence the PicoGUS-SB now reaches after the SDL/0106 graceful
            fall-back; if IRQ-5 still never fires, the OpenDevice-DMA + this
-           line bracket exactly where the chip was last touched. */
+           line bracket exactly where the chip was last touched. SDL/0107: the
+           stereo-bit suffix now keys on the actual channel count (channels==2)
+           rather than DSP>=3, since the 8-bit path defaults to MONO. */
         doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 DSP start seq (8-bit): 0xD1(spkr-on) "
                          "0x40 tc=%d (rate=%d effective=%d) 0x48 block_size=%d "
                          "(bytes-1) 0x1C(8-bit autoinit)%s",
                          (int)time_constant, device->spec.freq, effective_rate,
                          block_size,
-                         (soundblaster_version >= 3) ? " +mixer0x0E stereo-bit" : "");
+                         (device->spec.channels == 2) ? " +mixer0x0E stereo-bit" : "");
+
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0107): 8-bit channel-mode + silence-prime witness.
+           The decisive line for the PicoGUS-SB fix iter -- build-qa/g2k read it
+           to confirm the 8-bit device opened MONO (ch=1, effective == freq, no
+           0x0E stereo bit) and that the ring was silence-primed to U8 0x80.
+           Emits only on the 8-bit path (DOSBox-X emulates SB16 so it will not
+           fire under the default smoke -- optional banner; g2k PicoGUS-SB is
+           where it appears). Names the killswitch for the operator. */
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0107 8-bit channel mode: ch=%d (%s) tc=%d "
+                         "effective=%d Hz stereo_bit=%s ring_silence_primed=yes "
+                         "(killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_8BIT_STEREO=1 "
+                         "restores SB-Pro stereo)",
+                         device->spec.channels,
+                         (device->spec.channels == 2) ? "STEREO" : "MONO",
+                         (int)time_constant, effective_rate,
+                         (device->spec.channels == 2) ? "yes" : "no");
     }
 
     SDL_Log("SoundBlaster opened!");
-- 
